Here's a step-by-step guide to setting up a ROS 2 node in Python that subscribes to a laser scan topic and publishes velocity commands for obstacle avoidance:

### Step 1: Install ROS 2 and required packages

First, you need to install ROS 2 and the required packages. You can do this by running the following commands in your terminal:

```bash
# Install ROS 2
sudo apt update
sudo apt install curl
curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros/rosdistro/master/ros.asc | sudo apt-key add -
sudo sh -c 'echo "deb [arch=amd64] http://packages.ros.org/ros2/ubuntu $(lsb_release -sc) main" > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ros2-latest.list'
sudo apt update
sudo apt install ros-<distro>-ros2-foxy-desktop

# Install required packages
sudo apt install ros-<distro>-ros2-foxy-geometry2 ros-<distro>-ros2-foxy-geometry-msgs
```

Replace `<distro>` with the ROS 2 distribution you are using (e.g., `foxy`, `galactic`, etc.).

